{"type":"message","id":"41577438","parentId":"7ddb688d","timestamp":"2026-06-18T02:39:39.758Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking whether adding emoji to the config file would affect the code. This is a reasonable concern - can YAML handle emoji characters properly, and would Python read them correctly? Let me think about this...\n\nYAML supports UTF-8 natively, and Python can read emoji from YAML without issues. The emoji are just Unicode characters. The current code hardcodes emoji in Python dicts as strings like `\"👑\"`, so reading them from YAML instead would work identically.\n\nNo risk here - emoji in YAML is perfectly fine.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"不会。YAML 原生支持 UTF-8，emoji 就是普通 Unicode 字符。现在代码里 `\"BTC\": \"👑\"` 也是字符串，从 yaml 读进来是同一个东西。Python 的 `yaml.safe_load()` 对 emoji 完全没意见，不需要任何特殊处理。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":454,"output":309,"cacheRead":31488,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32251,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1781750374880}}
